  "findings": [
    "Exact-SHA inventory passed. Desktop build, plugin renderer, and loaded-plugin workflows passed on all three OSes; Rust CI passed workspace tests, format, Clippy, layering and native preview builds on Ubuntu, macOS, and Windows, plus the Rust 1.95 MSRV job.",
    "Quality failed its Knip audit on Ubuntu, macOS, and Windows because pbcopy, used by the round-trip audit script, was missing from knip.json ignoreBinaries. The parallel Fallow health audit passed on all three platforms.",
    "Pinned Obsidian 1.14.4 round-trip passed on Linux. Its report confirms the native Canvas text edit and exact Canvas-to-Markdown note creation flow, with source/note checks and reopen behavior passing.",
    "On macOS, Canvas text editing and explicit Save passed. The later note-creation flow set the expected Notes/Canvas text card.md destination and clipboard readback was exact; the screenshot visibly shows the correct field value, but Tesseract returned 'Notes/Canvas text card mq', so the OCR gate failed before Preview and no note was created.",
    "On Windows, Canvas field path and card ID readbacks passed, and loading the text draft made no vault changes. SendKeys failed exact readback on the 42-character draft at chunk offset 24 (expected prefix length 32, observed value length 28). The audit stopped before Save; the Canvas source stayed unchanged.",
    "The next focused fixes add pbcopy to the Knip binary allow-list, verify Windows keyboard input one character at a time before Save, and accept the observed one-character Tesseract misread at the .md suffix only when exact clipboard readback matches. All executable validation remains GitHub Actions only."
  ],
